  "control": "The same procedure run with the executor of the previous pin, the Ptah v0.18.0 release image, reproduced every checked-in reading record for record. The v0.22.0 image reproduced every MySQL reading but the allowed Apply's, both migration History readings and both restored-history refusals. It changed every PostgreSQL schema reading: each read of information_schema is now a read of pg_catalog, so the result no longer depends on the connecting role (stokaro/ptah#5499), and each command sends two reads more, of pg_inherits (stokaro/ptah#5341) and of the relations an extension owns (stokaro/ptah#5409). Planned statements lost their comment lines and a dropped table its IF EXISTS and CASCADE (stokaro/ptah#5341), which is what moved the allowed Apply on MySQL. All four saved exclusion plans carry that style and the scope Ptah has recorded since v0.19.0 (stokaro/ptah#5239).",
